 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ENTITY-ARMOR-TINT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY CLMODELS.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ROW-AREA            PIC X(66).
 01 WS-ITEM-ROW            PIC X(270).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG VALUE 10.5.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG VALUE 10.5.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I-D                 PIC 99.
 01 WS-LAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-S                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ITEM                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SLOT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ASSET               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CODE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MODEL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RED                 FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-GREEN               FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-BLUE                FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(64).
 01 WS-K20                 PIC X(24).
 01 WS-BASE-COUNT          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WANT-R             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WANT-G             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WANT-B             BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 0 TO PK-COUNT
     CALL "ENTITY-ATLAS-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     MOVE "zombie" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ID
     CALL "MM-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW
*>   A leather helmet (head slot, EN-EQ 6): undyed it is brown (A06540), dyed 00FF00 green, a stored 0 is undyed again (54 section 17, 43 section 7.2).
     MOVE "leather_helmet" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ITEM WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-ITEM TO EN-EQ(1, 6)
     MOVE 160 TO WS-WANT-R
     MOVE 101 TO WS-WANT-G
     MOVE 64 TO WS-WANT-B
     MOVE "armor tint an undyed leather helmet is brown A06540" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM CHECK-HEAD-TINT
     MOVE 65280 TO EN-EQ-DYE(1, 6)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-WANT-R WS-WANT-B
     MOVE 255 TO WS-WANT-G
     MOVE "armor tint a leather helmet dyed 00FF00 is green" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM CHECK-HEAD-TINT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-EQ-DYE(1, 6)
     MOVE 160 TO WS-WANT-R
     MOVE 101 TO WS-WANT-G
     MOVE 64 TO WS-WANT-B
     MOVE "armor tint a stored dye of 0 falls back to the undyed brown" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM CHECK-HEAD-TINT
*>   An iron helmet is never tinted, whatever its dye; the overlay layer count of the other layers is untouched.
     MOVE "iron_helmet" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ITEM WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-ITEM TO EN-EQ(1, 6)
     MOVE 65280 TO EN-EQ-DYE(1, 6)
     MOVE 255 TO WS-WANT-R WS-WANT-G WS-WANT-B
     MOVE "armor tint an iron helmet is white" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM CHECK-HEAD-TINT
*>   Leather boots (slot 2, EN-EQ 3, layer 7) take their own dye.
     MOVE "leather_boots" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ITEM WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-ITEM TO EN-EQ(1, 3)
     MOVE 16711680 TO EN-EQ-DYE(1, 3)
     CALL "ENTITY-OVERLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE 1 7 WS-CODE WS-RED WS-GREEN WS-BLUE WS-MODEL
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "armor tint leather boots dyed FF0000 are red" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 255 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = WS-RED * 255 - WS-GREEN * 255 - WS-BLUE * 255
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

 CHECK-HEAD-TINT.
     CALL "ENTITY-OVERLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE 1 8 WS-CODE WS-RED WS-GREEN WS-BLUE WS-MODEL
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = WS-WANT-R * 65536 + WS-WANT-G * 256 + WS-WANT-B
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = FUNCTION INTEGER(WS-RED * 255 + 0.5) * 65536 + FUNCTION INTEGER(WS-GREEN * 255 + 0.5) * 256
         + FUNCTION INTEGER(WS-BLUE * 255 + 0.5)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ENTITY-ARMOR-TINT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. MM-SPAWN.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, type (registry id), x y z (FLOAT-LONG), yaw (FLOAT-SHORT, also the head yaw): Add Entity.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-ADD                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-UUID                PIC X(16) VALUE LOW-VALUES.
 01 WS-V0                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V1                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V2                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-A0                  FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-X                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Y                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Z                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-YAW                  FLOAT-SHORT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-TYPE L-X L-Y L-Z L-YAW.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER WS-UUID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-TYPE
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-X
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Y
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER WS-V0 WS-V1 WS-V2
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-ADD
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM MM-SPAWN.

